WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.978
Week 23: Perfect Tenses and Relevant Past. report experience and recent developments connect past action to present relevance sequence prior events

2
00:00:09.978 --> 00:00:18.399
Form and meaning. Present perfect; past participles; regional preterite/perfect preferences; pluperfect introduction.

3
00:00:18.399 --> 00:00:45.915
Model set. Ya hemos completado la primera fase. Todavía no han llegado los datos. ¿Alguna vez has trabajado en Chile? Cuando llamó, yo ya había enviado el informe. La situación ha cambiado recientemente. We have already completed the first phase. The data have not arrived yet. Have you ever worked in Chile? When he or she called, I had already sent the report. The situation has changed recently.

4
00:00:45.915 --> 00:00:56.045
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:56.045 --> 00:01:10.442
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: report experience and recent developments; connect past action to present relevance; sequence prior events. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:10.442 --> 00:01:38.961
Model language. Ya hemos completado la primera fase. — We have already completed the first phase. Todavía no han llegado los datos. — The data have not arrived yet. ¿Alguna vez has trabajado en Chile? — Have you ever worked in Chile? Cuando llamó, yo ya había enviado el informe. — When he or she called, I had already sent the report. La situación ha cambiado recientemente. — The situation has changed recently.

7
00:01:38.961 --> 00:01:48.710
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
